                <div class="col-lg-7 pl-50">
                    <h2 class="new-head">CMA USA Requirements
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        To enroll for CMA USA course IMA requires candidates to –

                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Minimum be enrolled with an accredited university or college to pursue a bachelor’s degree (Or) Have a graduation degree from an accredited college or university

                    </p>
                    <h4 class="new-sub">However, to qualify as a CMA, IMA requires candidates to meet the following requirements –

                    </h4>
                    <ul class="about__info-list list-wrap">

                        <li class="about__info-list-item">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-play"></i>Be an active member of IMA and clear both CMA USA Parts 1 and 2 Exams

                        </li>
                        <li class="about__info-list-item">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-play"></i>To be a graduate from an accredited college/university or a related professional certification


                        </li>
                        <li class="about__info-list-item">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-play"></i>To follow IMA's Statement of Ethical Professional Practice and



                        </li>
                        <li class="about__info-list-item">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-play"></i>Have a minimum of two continuous years of full time work experience related to accounting and finance.



                        </li>
                      
                    </ul>
                    <p class="mt-2">The candidate once becomes an active member of IMA, have to attempt minimum one part exam before 12 months of registration and the duration provided by IMA for clearing both Part 1 and 2 Exams is three years.

</p>
